## What to double

| Dependency | Use | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Ports owned by this workspace (repositories, UoW, gateways) | **Fake** (in-memory, keeps the contract) | `{{fake_example}}` |
| External edges (HTTP, SDKs, clock, random) | Mock / stub at the edge | `{{mock_example}}` |
| The subject under test | **Never** | — |
| Authorization guards, the database | **Never mocked away** — keep the rule in a fake or cover with integration tests | — |

A double keeps the real contract: same return types, same errors raised for the same situations.

## Existing setup to reuse

- Framework: {{framework}} — no second framework, no global overrides ({{forbidden_overrides}}).
- Fixtures / factories: `{{fixtures_path}}`
- Existing fakes: `{{fakes_path}}`

## Isolation

No live network, database, file system or real clock in unit tests ({{isolation_notes}}).

